<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-21T17:40:44+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:40:44 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Delaware marked its state parks' 75th anniversary by planting its 75,000th tree, completing a five-year goal across 17 parks]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135087278.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Delaware celebrates the planting of its 75,000th tree in state parks, coinciding with the park system's 75th anniversary. This achievement contributes to a larger goal of planting one million trees by 2030. The initiative features diverse tree species, driven by the support of community volunteers. Notable trees like the American holly were chosen to improve environmental quality and provide inviting spaces for the public.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/delaware-marked-its-state-parks-75th-anniversary-by-planting-its-75000th-tree-completing-a-five-year-goal-across-17-parks-while-a-broader-program-aims-for-one-million-new-trees-by-2030/articleshow/135087278.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/delaware-marked-its-state-parks-75th-anniversary-by-planting-its-75000th-tree-completing-a-five-year-goal-across-17-parks-while-a-broader-program-aims-for-one-million-new-trees-by-2030/articleshow/135087278.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T17:02:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135087353,imgsize-1419286.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lonnie Mack’s iconic Flying V guitar and amplifier sell for $550,000 at auction]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135089878.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The legendary 1958 Gibson Flying V guitar, famously owned by Lonnie Mack and dubbed 'Number 7', fetched an impressive $550,000 at auction. This auction also featured Mack's 1962 Magnatone Custom 440 amplifier, which was crucial to his distinct sound. Mack's guitar, tailored for his innovative techniques, has had a profound influence on blues-rock music for many years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-late-1950s-guitarist-lonnie-mack-began-using-one-of-the-earliest-gibson-flying-v-guitars-after-decades-of-concerts-and-recordings-his-famous-number-7-and-an-amplifier-sold-together-for-550000-in-2026/articleshow/135089878.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-late-1950s-guitarist-lonnie-mack-began-using-one-of-the-earliest-gibson-flying-v-guitars-after-decades-of-concerts-and-recordings-his-famous-number-7-and-an-amplifier-sold-together-for-550000-in-2026/articleshow/135089878.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135090147,imgsize-777070.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After son’s death, mother’s support group now helps 7,000 men weekly]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135090228.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/after-her-son-died-at-23-in-2016-elaine-roberts-and-son-in-law-luke-ambler-started-a-mens-support-group-with-nine-attendees-today-it-helps-7000-men-a-week-and-has-earned-a-national-award/articleshow/135090228.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/after-her-son-died-at-23-in-2016-elaine-roberts-and-son-in-law-luke-ambler-started-a-mens-support-group-with-nine-attendees-today-it-helps-7000-men-a-week-and-has-earned-a-national-award/articleshow/135090228.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135090422,imgsize-624074.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dave Bautista borrowed money for Christmas gifts before WWE and Hollywood fame]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135089725.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/dave-bautista-worked-as-a-bouncer-and-borrowed-money-for-his-daughters-christmas-gifts-before-becoming-a-wwe-star-he-later-built-a-second-career-as-a-hollywood-actor/articleshow/135089725.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/dave-bautista-worked-as-a-bouncer-and-borrowed-money-for-his-daughters-christmas-gifts-before-becoming-a-wwe-star-he-later-built-a-second-career-as-a-hollywood-actor/articleshow/135089725.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T16:19:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135089922,imgsize-643589.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Virginia is turning 100,000 tons of demolished bridge concrete into fish habitat; 951 tons already underwater]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135062470.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Hampton Roads Bridge-Tunnel expansion project involves dismantling an old bridge and using the concrete for artificial reefs. This initiative helps divert demolition waste from landfills while enhancing underwater habitats. Approximately 100,000 tons of concrete is expected to be repurposed for marine life by 2027. The Virginia Marine Resources Commission manages the artificial reefs that support local fisheries and marine ecosystems. This innovative approach connects infrastructure development with environmental sustainability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/virginia-is-dismantling-100000-tons-of-concrete-from-its-3-9-billion-hampton-roads-bridge-tunnel-expansion-951-tons-have-already-been-placed-underwater-as-part-of-a-project-to-build-fish-habitat-in-chesapeake-bay/articleshow/135062470.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/virginia-is-dismantling-100000-tons-of-concrete-from-its-3-9-billion-hampton-roads-bridge-tunnel-expansion-951-tons-have-already-been-placed-underwater-as-part-of-a-project-to-build-fish-habitat-in-chesapeake-bay/articleshow/135062470.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T16:06:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135062478,imgsize-1076385.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Swiss brothers spend £10,000 creating a Greek village in their garden]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135088607.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/two-swiss-brothers-spent-about-10000-turning-a-15-by-15-metre-section-of-their-garden-into-a-miniature-greek-village-with-blue-shutters-stone-lanes-and-a-bar-the-wider-backyard-attraction-cost-20000/articleshow/135088607.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/two-swiss-brothers-spent-about-10000-turning-a-15-by-15-metre-section-of-their-garden-into-a-miniature-greek-village-with-blue-shutters-stone-lanes-and-a-bar-the-wider-backyard-attraction-cost-20000/articleshow/135088607.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135088850,imgsize-934449.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia releases 50 critically endangered smoky mice into forest after decades of absence]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135085964.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Australia has successfully reintroduced almost 50 critically endangered smoky mice into South East Forest National Park. This reintroduction represents a significant step towards restoring the region’s ecosystem and native mammal populations. Various species, including the long-footed potoroo and eastern quoll, are also planned for reintroduction. The effort is part of a broader initiative by the NSW Government and conservationists.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/australia-releases-nearly-50-critically-endangered-smoky-mice-into-a-predator-free-forest-where-the-species-had-not-been-seen-since-the-1990s/articleshow/135085964.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/australia-releases-nearly-50-critically-endangered-smoky-mice-into-a-predator-free-forest-where-the-species-had-not-been-seen-since-the-1990s/articleshow/135085964.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T16:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135086021,imgsize-109793.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ukraine peace, prisoner release &amp; Trump meeting: What was discussed in Putin's meeting with US envoy Witkoff]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135088653.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Vladimir Putin met with US special envoy Steve Witkoff to discuss potential solutions to the Ukraine conflict. Witkoff presented proposals aimed at reviving negotiations between Russia and Ukraine, emphasizing the need for trilateral talks. During the meeting, they addressed the release of Stephen Hubbard, an American prisoner in Russia, and issues related to economic cooperation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-peace-prisoner-release-trump-meeting-what-was-discussed-in-putins-meeting-with-us-envoy-witkoff/articleshow/135088653.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-peace-prisoner-release-trump-meeting-what-was-discussed-in-putins-meeting-with-us-envoy-witkoff/articleshow/135088653.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T15:47:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https